{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>Therefore he called his name, etc.</b> That is, Esav himself called his name Edom — and the reason was not because he said ״הָאָדֹם הָאָדֹם״ twice, but rather because he had been on the verge of death and through it he revived his soul, so he called his name Edom after his own name. And Esav was precise in names, as he said (Genesis 27:36): ״הֲכִי קָרָא שְׁמוֹ״, etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:43:20.079205577Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}